    "collapsible_content_n7Ak9U": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_n6tG6B": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Q1. What is the best herbal tea for winding down in the evening?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Herbs such as chamomile, linden and passion flower have long been enjoyed in evening infusions to accompany a moment of stillness after a busy day. At Thea Botanicals we blend herbs like these into loose leaf teas designed for the quiet ritual of winding down, rather than for any specific medical outcome.<br/><br/></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_fGi8ir": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Q2. Why do people enjoy chamomile tea?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Chamomile has been used for centuries as a gentle evening infusion, valued for its soft, apple-like flavour and its traditional association with rest and ease. It sits at the heart of our Calm Tea No.01, for those seeking a calmer way to close the day.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Xh68eG": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Q3. Is loose leaf tea better quality than tea bags?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Loose leaf tea generally contains whole or larger pieces of herb, which can allow a fuller flavour and a more generous infusion. This is why our blends are made as loose leaf, favouring depth of flavour over convenience.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_yPxRXV": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Q4. Which herbs are traditionally enjoyed for moments of rest?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Herbs such as chamomile, linden, passion flower and lemon verbena have traditionally been enjoyed to accompany moments of rest and quiet reflection. All four appear in our Calm Tea No.01, combined thoughtfully for flavour as well as ritual.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_eddLDC": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Q5. Is organic tea actually better than non-organic tea?",
            "icon": "question_mark",
            "row_content": "<p>Organic herbs are grown without synthetic pesticides, which many people find reassuring when choosing something they'll drink daily. Our herbs come from certified organic suppliers, and we're always happy to answer questions about where they're from.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
